# Plan §7b "Локальные объявления и явная инициализация" (the author, docs/new_parts/local_declarations_and_explicit_
# initialization.to_fable.en.md §2, §3, §5 items 1-3; Q51): computed initialization is two ordinary statements, `int: i`
# then `i: findValue` -- a callable named where a value is consumed gives its result, so the assignment calls findValue
# when control reaches it and only then.  M(0) skips the line: no call.  M(2) reaches it twice: each time one call, and
# the same local i takes the new result (41, then 42) -- no second declaration, no snapshot.  A path from outside, M\i,
# reads the place of declaration: during M (peek, after the call's checkpoint published i) and after it -- and reading
# it executes nothing.  findValue and count reach the unit's calls by an explicit path (Q52: a bare write would be the
# callee's hidden input; the root's bare calls is its own working value).  The root's own `int: z` / `z: findValue` is
# the same statement pair at the root: 43.  a 0, c0 0, b 424142 (i 42, peek saw 41 then 42), after 42, z 43, calls 3.
# Success 7; a call on the skipped line 65; a read that runs the call 66; any other value 64.
int: calls 0
fn: findValue () int
    node\calls: node\calls + 1
    return: 40 + node\calls
end: findValue
fn: count () int
    return: node\calls
end: count
fn: peek () int
    return: M\i
end: peek
fn: M (int: go) int
    int: i
    int: seen 0
    while: go > 0
        i: findValue
        seen: seen * 100 + peek()
        go: go - 1
    return: i * 10000 + seen
end: M
int: a 0
a: M(0)
int: c0 0
c0: count()
int: b 0
b: M(2)
int: after 0
after: M\i
int: z
z: findValue
int: n 0
n: count()
int: ok 64
if: c0 != 0
    ok: 65
if: n > 3
    ok: 66
if: a = 0 && c0 = 0 && b = 424142 && after = 42 && z = 43 && n = 3
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
